cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalization, please cite the accompanying paper and this repository."
title: "StructuralBertrand: a Lean 4 / Mathlib formalization of a structural reduction of Bertrand's postulate"
abstract: >-
  A machine-checked (zero-`sorry`) Lean 4 development that reduces the
  Bertrand–Chebyshev theorem to a single positivity statement about an exact
  window count, derives the window and its endpoint from the prime base, and closes
  the residual quantitative atom with a self-contained argument on the central
  binomial coefficient. The main theorem does not import Mathlib's proof of
  Bertrand's postulate.
type: software
authors:
